From: Kettle Linux <kettlelinux@kettlelinux.org>
Subject: [PATCH] remoteproc: qcom_q6v5: log a repeated handover at debug level

Once the handover has happened the proxy votes are released, so a later
handover interrupt changes nothing. The SM8550 ADSP raises it every ~180 ms
while its Sensor Core streams (the motion sensors, through hexagonrpcd and
libssc), and each one logged an error. Log it at debug level.
---
--- a/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5.c
+++ b/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5.c
@@ -165,7 +165,7 @@
 	struct qcom_q6v5 *q6v5 = data;
 
 	if (q6v5->handover_issued) {
-		dev_err(q6v5->dev, "Handover signaled, but it already happened\n");
+		dev_dbg(q6v5->dev, "Handover signaled, but it already happened\n");
 		return IRQ_HANDLED;
 	}
 
